  Contemporary Figure: Dan Flood (Security Professional)

  In recent news (as of September 2025), Dan Flood refers to a modern security
  expert, formerly

  with Shaffer Security Group and now associated with Turning Point USA (TUSA)
  as head of

  security. He's drawn scrutiny amid conspiracy theories surrounding the
  September 10, 2025,

  assassination of conservative activist Charlie Kirk at a Utah Valley
  University event.

  • Professional Background: Flood has ties to counterterrorism training,
  including

  programs with the Jewish Institute for National Security of America (JINSA),
  which

  facilitates U.S.-Israeli security exchanges. He reportedly hired Integrity
  Security Solutions

  (led by Brian Harpole) for the UVU event. Greg Shaffer, his former employer,
  accused

  Flood of "stabbing him in the back" by poaching clients like TPUSA.

  • Current Controversy: Online discussions, particularly on X, allege Flood's
  involvement in

  Kirk's death-citing video footage of him signaling, stepping back, and
  photographing the

  scene. These claims remain unverified speculation, with no official charges or
  FBI

  statements implicating him. Flood has no public social media presence since
  the incident

  and hasn't commented publicly.
